<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
     STATIC APP SHORTCUTS (Stage D task 1, N3 — dist/round5-options.html #batch:
     "Start <last routine>" / "Log measurement" / "Progress photos", long-press the
     launcher icon). Registered via the <meta-data android:name="android.app.shortcuts">
     entry on the LauncherOpenPump activity-alias in AndroidManifest.xml (incognito, 0.10:
     the launcher entries are aliases of LauncherTrampoline now; each disguise's - "Fitness
     log", "Habits", "Notes" - carries its own file, shortcuts_fitness.xml,
     shortcuts_habits.xml and shortcuts_notes.xml: the same three with its own icon).

     THIS IS THE ONE CORRECT USE OF A PLATFORM RESOURCE XML in an app that otherwise
     builds every screen in code — a launcher shortcut is a system-level surface Android
     reads before this app's process (or any of its own UI) exists at all, so it cannot
     be anything OTHER than a manifest-adjacent resource. Nothing about "no XML layouts"
     is violated: no screen is defined here, only three system entry points into the ones
     SessionActivity already builds.

     Ignored outright on API < 25 (ShortcutManager does not exist there) — this app's
     minSdk is 24, and a shortcut that silently does not appear on the oldest supported
     devices is the correct degrade, not a crash.

     EACH <intent> targets ShortcutTrampoline (re-review 4), never SessionActivity: Android
     starts a static shortcut with NEW_TASK | CLEAR_TASK, which on SessionActivity cleared the
     running screen's task and ended a run in its onDestroy. The trampoline has its own task
     affinity, so the clear takes only its own task, and it forwards the extra below to the
     one SessionActivity (see the manifest's note on it).

     EACH <intent> names its target BY EXPLICIT COMPONENT (targetPackage +
     targetClass), so it needs no matching <intent-filter> — explicit-component intents
     bypass intent-filter resolution entirely. The single <extra> on each names which of
     the three the tap was, read in SessionActivity#onCreate/#onNewIntent via the shared
     EXTRA_SHORTCUT key (see SessionActivity#handleShortcutIntent).

     "Start last routine" cannot literally name the routine: static shortcuts carry
     PRE-COMPILED labels with no way to interpolate live app state (that needs DYNAMIC
     shortcuts, a bigger feature nothing here asks for), so the label stays generic and
     the routine it starts is resolved at tap time by Model#lastRunRoutineId.
-->
<shortcuts xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <shortcut
        android:shortcutId="start_last_routine"
        android:enabled="true"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_start_last_short"
        android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_start_last_long">
        <intent
            android:action="android.intent.action.VIEW"
            android:targetPackage="org.openpump"
            android:targetClass="org.openpump.ShortcutTrampoline">
            <extra android:name="org.openpump.SHORTCUT_ACTION" android:value="start_last" />
        </intent>
    </shortcut>
    <shortcut
        android:shortcutId="log_measurement"
        android:enabled="true"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_log_measurement_short"
        android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_log_measurement_long">
        <intent
            android:action="android.intent.action.VIEW"
            android:targetPackage="org.openpump"
            android:targetClass="org.openpump.ShortcutTrampoline">
            <extra android:name="org.openpump.SHORTCUT_ACTION" android:value="log_measurement" />
        </intent>
    </shortcut>
    <shortcut
        android:shortcutId="progress_photos"
        android:enabled="true"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_progress_photos_short"
        android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_progress_photos_long">
        <intent
            android:action="android.intent.action.VIEW"
            android:targetPackage="org.openpump"
            android:targetClass="org.openpump.ShortcutTrampoline">
            <extra android:name="org.openpump.SHORTCUT_ACTION" android:value="progress_photos" />
        </intent>
    </shortcut>
</shortcuts>
